  "body": "Found in the delta safety read of PR #3284 (#2604). The two are safe: the output is correct or refused. (1) `crates/app/src/tool_reservations.rs:67-69`: a second probe is refused when all pockets that are reserved for a probe are in use; it does not take a free number. Say what the user must do in the refusal text, or permit a free pocket. (2) `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings.rs:278`: the window shows a `next_free` number that does not look at the reservations of the machine; the command then refuses or takes a different number. Use the same allocation as the command. (3) The refusal text shows the word `tool_setter` as it is in the file; give it a plain name.",
